# Fictional EP Tracklist

## 1. Treble Strings Fail Before the Gauge Returns

**Story & Context:** The debut runs at 130 BPM. Oksana opens with a wide bandura sweep spanning treble and bass registers. The high strings decay in less than a second while the lower strings continue to ring. Mira places no kick under the initial STRIKE. Instead, one brittle snare appears just after the high strings disappear, followed by a short sub pulse only when the bass resonance reaches VOID.

Iryna places one glass-marimba suspended second during RESIDUE. Taras replaces the next programmed kick with a hand-damped bass-drum thud. Jon remains silent until the third cycle, then adds one breath-heavy low recorder tone after Oksana mutes the bass strings earlier than expected.

At the midpoint, Oksana repeats the same sweep but manually damps the low strings first, reversing the normal decay hierarchy. Mira responds by bringing the sub in earlier while withholding the snare. The track ends with one treble cluster whose final ringing string survives longer than expected; the ensemble waits for it to disappear before stopping.

