## 2. Specimen Glass Rings After the Kick Is Deleted

**Story & Context:** At 134 BPM, Mira begins with the EP's most direct club pattern but removes every fourth kick. Oksana fills none of those vacancies. Instead, the missing low impact creates a VOID into which Iryna places a single glass-marimba fifth. The result makes the brittle pitched attack feel larger than a conventional drum hit.

Taras answers alternate missing kicks with one prepared-bass-drum stroke, producing a cycle of electronic kick, silence-plus-glass, electronic kick, acoustic low shock. Oksana plays short two-note bandura figures only in the spaces between these four-state cycles. Jon adds unpitched recorder air rather than notes for the first half.

In the final minute, Mira removes the remaining electronic kicks one by one while Taras keeps only two acoustic low events per eight bars. The dance pulse survives through expectation, string attack, and glass placement rather than continuous bass drum.

